#
# Tchibo Weather Station TCM220063 Sub-GHz Script
# Compatible with Flipper Zero Weather App
#
# Device Information:
# - Model: TCM220063 (Tchibo/TCM brand)
# - Frequency: 433.92 MHz
# - Modulation: OOK (On-Off Keying)
# - Data Rate: ~1 kbps
# - Transmission Interval: Every 60 seconds
# - Range: Up to 100 meters (line of sight)
#
# Protocol Details:
# - Based on Nexus Weather Protocol
# - Packet Length: 36 bits
# - Manchester encoding
# - Preamble: 12 bits alternating pattern
# - Sync word: 4 bits
# - Data payload: 32 bits
# - No CRC (checksum calculated differently)
#
# Data Packet Structure (32 bits after preamble/sync):
# Bits 0-3:   Channel ID (0-2, typically 0)
# Bits 4-11:  Rolling code/Random ID (changes on battery replacement)
# Bits 12-23: Temperature (signed 12-bit, 0.1°C resolution, offset +40°C)
# Bits 24-31: Humidity (8-bit, 0-100%)
#
# Temperature Calculation:
# Raw value represents (temperature + 40.0) * 10
# Example: Raw 235 = (23.5 - 40.0) = -16.5°C
#          Raw 450 = (45.0 - 40.0) = 5.0°C
#
# Example Transmissions:
